Admin Dashboard API Documentation
Overview
This document describes the APIs used by the Admin Dashboard to manage and monitor
membership-related data such as purchases, redemptions, and transactions.
All APIs require authentication using a JWT token obtained after successful login. Only
users with the role ADDHEAD are authorized to access these endpoints.
Authentication Flow
1. Request OTP (Admin Login)
Initiates login by sending an OTP to the registered mobile number.
• Endpoint: /api/users/login/request-otp
• Method: POST
• Headers:
o Content-Type: application/json
• Request Body:
{
 "mobileNumber": "9876543210"
}
• Response:
{
 "message": "OTP sent successfully"
}
2. Verify OTP (Admin Login)
Verifies OTP and returns JWT token for authenticated requests.
• Endpoint: /api/users/login/verify-otp
• Method: POST
• Headers:
o Content-Type: application/json
• Request Body:
{
 "mobileNumber": "9876543210",
 "otp": "1234"
}
• Response:
{
 "message": "Login successful",
 "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR...",
 "user": {},
 "role": "ADDHEAD"
}
 Use the returned token as a Bearer token in all subsequent API requests.
Admin APIs
3. Get All Active Memberships
Fetches a paginated list of all membership purchases across the platform.
• Endpoint: /api/membership/admin/all
• Method: GET
• Query Parameters:
o page (number) – Page number (default: 1)
o limit (number) – Items per page (default: 20)
o search (string) – Search by name/mobile (optional)
• Headers:
o Authorization: Bearer <token>
• Example Request:
/api/membership/admin/all?page=1&limit=20&search=
• Response:
{
 "memberships": [],
 "totalPages": 5,
 "currentPage": 1,
 "totalItems": 100
}
4. Get All Redemptions
Fetches a paginated list of all service redemptions.
• Endpoint: /api/membership/admin/redemptions
• Method: GET
• Query Parameters:
o page (number)
o limit (number)
o search (string)
• Headers:
o Authorization: Bearer <token>
• Example Request:
/api/membership/admin/redemptions?page=1&limit=20&search=
• Response:
{
 "redemptions": [],
 "totalPages": 2,
 "currentPage": 1,
 "totalItems": 35
}
5. Get Recent Transactions (Activity Feed)
Fetches a combined chronological list of purchases and redemptions.
• Endpoint: /api/membership/admin/transactions
• Method: GET
• Query Parameters:
o limit (number) – Number of records to fetch
• Headers:
o Authorization: Bearer <token>
• Example Request:
/api/membership/admin/transactions?limit=20
• Response:
[
 {
 "type": "Redemption",
 "date": "2026-04-22T06:00:00.000Z",
 "mobileNumber": "9876543210",
 "name": "Gold Membership",
 "details": "Redeemed Haircut",
 "amount": 200,
 "id": "69a1b2c3d..."
 },
 {
 "type": "Purchase",
 "date": "2026-04-22T05:30:00.000Z",
 "mobileNumber": "9876543210",
 "name": "John Doe",
 "details": "Purchased Gold Membership",
 "amount": 1000,
 "id": "67f8a12b3..."
 }
]
Error Handling
All APIs may return the following error responses:
Unauthorized Access
{
 "message": "Unauthorized"
}
Invalid Token
{
 "message": "Invalid or expired token"
}
Validation Error
{
 "message": "Invalid request parameters"
}
Notes
• All timestamps are in ISO 8601 format (UTC)
• Pagination should be handled at the frontend level
• Ensure secure storage of JWT tokens
• Role-based access is strictly enforced (ADDHEAD only)
Conclusion
These APIs enable the Admin Dashboard to:
• Monitor memberships
• Track redemptions
• View real-time transaction activity
Ensure proper authentication and parameter handling for seamless integration.